{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1948 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b3ad466376e496a91be4ae5d98a9844b75f1bb3bb6e50114e8a6946f5ab3f3c1" :edb/db-before-t 1947 :edb/db-after-t 1948 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535260 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:37:14.041Z" 13194139535260 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340391 13194139535260 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340420 13194139535260 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340405 13194139535260 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340412 13194139535260 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340416 13194139535260 true] [17592186100853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340398 13194139535260 true] [17592186100853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340428 13194139535260 true] [17592186299141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340415 13194139535260 true] [17592186340391 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340392 13194139535260 true] [17592186340391 1089 "q-12380" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340391 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535260 true] [17592186340391 1100 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ about $x=0$ is" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340391 1113 #uuid "0115977e-e552-5c81-a528-e4c41764a6e8" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340391 1145 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-{e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=-1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =2{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-2{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1+(-1)\\cdot x+0\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(2)\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340393 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340394 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340395 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340396 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340397 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1041 "selection" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340394 13194139535260 true] [17592186340392 1110 #uuid "d8bc7550-2675-595b-b9dc-de2d38777602" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340393 1034 "x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{6}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340393 1111 #uuid "4d5f2a9c-51b9-539f-8c6e-ea1a085f1ceb" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340394 1034 "1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340394 1111 #uuid "46b04293-c25f-59e0-ab1f-a7bedcc3b909" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340395 1034 "x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340395 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340395 1111 #uuid "0cf1e140-3a61-5f1f-8474-573dd7ff2134" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340396 1034 "1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340396 1111 #uuid "b74a8e50-2478-5ef1-85ba-f9354727c79a" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340397 1034 "1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340397 1111 #uuid "f6b6fcfa-66e0-54c2-bbdc-5c5072eac42c" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340398 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340399 13194139535260 true] [17592186340398 1089 "q-125899" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340398 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535260 true] [17592186340398 1100 "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(7)=4,{f}^{′}(7)=2,{f}^{″}(7)=-6$ and ${f}^{‴}(7)=-24.$ Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=7?$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340398 1113 #uuid "bcf4e431-a952-5630-8441-62a79c4f1460" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340398 1145 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(7)+{f}^{′}(7)(x-7)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(7)}{2!}(x-7)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(7)}{3!}(x-7)^{3} \\\\  & =f(7)+{f}^{′}(7)(x-7)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(7)}{2}(x-7)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(7)}{6}(x-7)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(7) & =4 \\\\ {f}^{′}(7) & =2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(7) & =-6 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(7) & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =4+2(x-7)+\\frac{(-6)}{2}(x-7)^{2}+\\frac{(-24)}{6}(x-7)^{3} \\\\  & =4+2(x-7)-3(x-7)^{2}-4(x-7)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340400 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340401 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340402 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340403 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340404 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1041 "selection" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340403 13194139535260 true] [17592186340399 1110 #uuid "9c59e2e1-832e-53b5-8999-3e4baa093498" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340400 1034 "4+2(x-7)-3(x-7)^{2}-6(x-7)^{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340400 1111 #uuid "18e40568-8c1b-55ad-b445-ec0b5bb1110f" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340401 1034 "4+2(x-7)-(x-7)^{2}-6(x-7)^{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340401 1111 #uuid "f47222d5-df06-520f-a6d9-af61a4339cfe" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340402 1034 "4+2(x-7)-2(x-7)^{2}-8(x-7)^{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340402 1111 #uuid "a9e132c0-0d57-55ff-9add-2494b337d488" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340403 1034 "4+2(x-7)-3(x-7)^{2}-4(x-7)^{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340403 1111 #uuid "d1f61c9d-4905-50f0-8c64-7c0f6f4c4dc5" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340404 1034 "4+(x-7)-(x-7)^{2}-4(x-7)^{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340404 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340404 1111 #uuid "8c8c1bfd-417a-5c0f-b728-254b72d54479" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340405 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340406 13194139535260 true] [17592186340405 1089 "q-126357" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340405 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535260 true] [17592186340405 1100 "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x)$ about $x=0?$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340405 1113 #uuid "47beb5c7-b9f8-5cdc-a46a-e7eedfb53a9c" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340405 1145 "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{2-x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(2-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{(2-x)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=-\\frac{2}{(2-0)^{3}}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})=-\\frac{1}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $-\\frac{1}{24}.$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340407 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340408 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340409 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340410 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340411 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1041 "selection" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340411 13194139535260 true] [17592186340406 1110 #uuid "aebd5143-a59e-53a2-af4e-cac6cbdb03da" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340407 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340407 1111 #uuid "4a53711d-af4e-5cce-9fac-361accefdd42" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340408 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340408 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340408 1111 #uuid "34d30c09-f20e-5c1c-a5af-232ba2e16174" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340409 1034 "-\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340409 1111 #uuid "381e07d1-b15c-503d-ab39-f4bcedecd81d" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340410 1034 "\\frac{1}{48}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340410 1111 #uuid "a426abc4-a409-5441-8307-9894921ac337" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340411 1034 "-\\frac{1}{24}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340411 1111 #uuid "3c948602-d09f-5030-8b6f-b470b8936046" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340412 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340413 13194139535260 true] [17592186340412 1089 "q-348019" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340412 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535260 true] [17592186340412 1100 "Find the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+x)$ about $x=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535260 true] [17592186340412 1113 #uuid "56837e97-06d8-5989-94c8-2e9269703dbe" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340412 1145 "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+x) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2+x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(2+x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(2+x)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{2}{(2+0)^{3}}=\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{24}.$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340414 13194139535260 true] [17592186340413 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535260 true] [17592186340413 1041 "field-1" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340413 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340414 13194139535260 true] [17592186340413 1110 #uuid "1714e555-7ad7-52f7-aa9d-1acbe22fde82" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340414 1034 "\\frac{1}{24}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340414 1111 #uuid "1e24fd73-3730-544b-b72d-0d2cec8818fc" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340415 1034 "4" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340415 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340415 1111 #uuid "4c1088db-22d5-54b6-a598-f210b1474a68" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340416 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340417 13194139535260 true] [17592186340416 1089 "q-351869" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340416 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535260 true] [17592186340416 1100 "Find the coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ about $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535260 true] [17592186340416 1113 #uuid "962c443b-40cc-5a79-88ee-071a8061f1eb" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340416 1145 "The coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(3).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(3),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(3)=-\\frac{6}{{3}^{4}}=-\\frac{6}{81}=-\\frac{2}{27}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(3)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{27})=-\\frac{2}{6\\cdot 27}=-\\frac{1}{81}.\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ is $-\\frac{1}{81}.$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340417 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340418 13194139535260 true] [17592186340417 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340419 13194139535260 true] [17592186340417 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535260 true] [17592186340417 1041 "field-1" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340417 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340418 13194139535260 true] [17592186340417 1110 #uuid "e027e265-2e46-5698-a52e-62df8c16cb38" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340418 1034 "-\\frac{1}{81}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340418 1111 #uuid "038d5daa-95f1-5dbb-971a-a26686b08e71" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340419 1034 "\\frac{1}{81}" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535260 true] [17592186340419 1111 #uuid "de62eb2c-63f6-5372-a9ca-53858179ecf4" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340421 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340424 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340426 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1089 "q-351999" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1100 "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ about $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$(x-1)\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x-1)^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$(x-1)^{3}$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1113 #uuid "d447ff59-5163-5274-8987-8699bd1198dd" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340420 1145 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=1,$ we plug $a=1$ into the general formula to give \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2!}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{3!}(x-1)^{3} \\\\ {P}_{3}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{6}(x-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ and ${f}^{‴}(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & ⟹ &  & f(1) & =\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(1) & =-\\frac{2}{{1}^{3}}=-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(1) & =\\frac{6}{{1}^{4}}=6 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{24}{{x}^{5}} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(1) & =-\\frac{24}{{1}^{5}}=-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ and ${f}^{‴}(1)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =(1)+(-2)\\cdot (x-1)+\\frac{(6)}{2}\\cdot (x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(-24)}{6}\\cdot (x-1)^{3} \\\\  & =1-2(x-1)+3(x-1)^{2}-4(x-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340422 13194139535260 true] [17592186340421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340423 13194139535260 true] [17592186340421 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535260 true] [17592186340421 1041 "field-1" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340421 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340422 13194139535260 true] [17592186340421 1110 #uuid "eb3d9fdb-6377-5367-b531-9d53d7688c03" 13194139535260 true] [17592186340422 1